## lifecycle/real.rs (lead-owned)

Inside impl DiscoveryPublication, replace new/with_writer with the following three
functions. Keep all other methods and fields. Arc, mpsc, Job and CoreState already
exist in this file.

    pub fn new(root: PathBuf, base: Discovery, on_fatal: OnFatal) -> Self {
        let owned = Arc::new(discovery::OwnedDiscovery::start(root.clone()));
        let kept = owned.clone();
        let write: WriteDocument = Box::new(move |_root, document| kept.publish(document));
        Self::spawn(root, base, write, Some(owned), on_fatal)
    }

    fn with_writer(root: PathBuf, base: Discovery, write: WriteDocument, on_fatal: OnFatal) -> Self {
        Self::spawn(root, base, write, None, on_fatal)
    }

    fn spawn(
        root: PathBuf,
        base: Discovery,
        write: WriteDocument,
        owned: Option<Arc<discovery::OwnedDiscovery>>,
        on_fatal: OnFatal,
    ) -> Self {
        let (jobs, inbox) = mpsc::channel::<Job>();
        let instance_id = base.core.instance_id.clone();
        std::thread::Builder::new()
            .name("mixdog-discovery".into())
            .spawn(move || {
                for job in inbox {
                    match job {
                        Job::Publish(document) => {
                            if let Err(error) = write(&root, &document) {
                                tracing::error!(%error, "discovery was not published");
                                if document.core.state != CoreState::Draining { on_fatal(&error); }
                            }
                        }
                        Job::Barrier { withdraw, done } => {
                            if withdraw {
                                let withdrawn = match &owned {
                                    Some(owned) => owned.release(&instance_id),
                                    None => discovery::withdraw(&root, &instance_id),
                                };
                                if let Err(error) = withdrawn {
                                    tracing::error!(%error, "discovery was not withdrawn");
                                }
                            }
                            let _ = done.send(());
                        }
                    }
                }
            })
            .expect("the OS refused a discovery thread");
        Self { base, rpc: Mutex::new(None), jobs: Mutex::new(jobs) }
    }

## lifecycle/real_tests.rs integration assertion (lead-owned)

    #[test]
    fn a_deleted_discovery_file_comes_back_until_the_core_withdraws_it() {
        let root = tempfile::tempdir().unwrap();
        let publication = DiscoveryPublication::new(root.path().to_path_buf(), template(), Box::new(|_| {}));
        publication.publish(&DiscoveryState { phase: DiscoveryPhase::Serving, blocked: None, drain_id: None });
        publication.flush();
        let file = discovery::path(root.path());
        std::fs::remove_file(&file).unwrap();
        let deadline = std::time::Instant::now() + std::time::Duration::from_secs(10);
        while !file.is_file() {
            assert!(std::time::Instant::now() < deadline, "discovery was not restored");
            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(20));
        }
        publication.withdraw();
        std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(100));
        assert!(!file.exists());
    }

## Isolated full ensureCore exercise, implemented but NOT run

New ignored discovery::tests::ensure_core_reattaches_after_discovery_republication
spawns the current Rust test executable as a private helper. Its only state is a
temp runtime root. It does not run mixdogd, acquire a real profile, initialize a
store, bind a service, or signal/kill a process. The helper self-expires after 20s
and normally exits on a private stop marker. On Windows both helpers use hidden
creation flags. Test-only environment names never enter production behavior.

The Node harness imports the real packages/protocol-client/src/launch/ensure-core.mjs.
Its first ensureCore invokes the injected launch callback exactly once, opening a
start gate for the owned Rust child's real OwnedDiscovery publisher. It deletes
daemon.json, waits for restoration, calls ensureCore again, and checks the same
live child PID, serving state and one launch total. Cleanup asks only this owned
child to finish and waits for its normal exit. Node is a test oracle, not a product
fallback. No real core/profile is used.

After the dependency and real.rs wiring, root can run:
    cargo test -p mixdog-app-server-daemon --lib discovery::tests
    cargo test -p mixdog-app-server-daemon --lib discovery::tests::ensure_core_reattaches_after_discovery_republication -- --ignored --exact --nocapture

Also run the real_tests assertion above, existing lifecycle publication/fatal-write
checks, and lint. The ordinary discovery tests cover deletion immediately after
publish, root deletion, overwritten/malformed JSON, same-pid numeric-string/lone
surrogate JSON preservation, blocked contender exclusion, migrating ownership,
draining/release/drop. No Rust build/test, daemon, deployment or commit was run in
this corrective worktree; runtime event delivery and full integration remain gates.

Finding status: implemented (uncommitted), pending root wiring and the above tests.
